 <pekka.jaaskelainen@intel.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Dec 2022 19:23:56 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] Allow up to v1.2 SPIR-V features and pass only the
 necessary extensions

Raise the HIPSPV translator invocation from --spirv-max-version=1.1 to
1.3 so warp-level primitives (shuffles, ballots) are usable via the core (shuffles, ballots) are usable via the
Intel subgroup extensions (the non-extension forms would need v1.3,
which no target supports yet), and replace --spirv-ext=+all with an
explicit allowlist (SPV_INTEL_function_pointers, SPV_INTEL_subgroups,
SPV_EXT_shader_atomic_float_add) so the emitted SPIR-V only declares
extensions chipStar actually needs and consumers actually support.

Applies-to: LLVM release/22.x
Upstream-status: equivalent change upstreamed in LLVM 23+ gated on
Triple::ChipStar via llvm/llvm-project#179902 (0c8b435c57f6); still
needed on release/22.x, which branched before it.
---
 clang/lib/Driver/ToolChains/HIPSPV.cpp | 8 +++++---
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/clang/lib/Driver/ToolChains/HIPSPV.cpp b/clang/lib/Driver/ToolChains/HIPSPV.cpp
index f797573..4cde8f9 100644
--- a/clang/lib/Driver/ToolChains/HIPSPV.cpp
+++ b/clang/lib/Driver/ToolChains/HIPSPV.cpp
@@ -90,9 +90,11 @@ void HIPSPV::Linker::constructLinkAndEmitSpirvCommand(
   }
 
   // Emit SPIR-V binary.
-
-  llvm::opt::ArgStringList TrArgs{"--spirv-max-version=1.1",
-                                  "--spirv-ext=+all"};
+  // We need 1.2 when using warp-level primitivies via sub group extensions.
+  // Strictly put we'd need 1.3 for the standard non-extension shuffle
+  // operations, but it's not supported by any target yet.
+  llvm::opt::ArgStringList TrArgs{"--spirv-max-version=1.3",
+                                  "--spirv-ext=-all,+SPV_INTEL_function_pointers,+SPV_INTEL_subgroups,+SPV_EXT_shader_atomic_float_add"};
   InputInfo TrInput = InputInfo(types::TY_LLVM_BC, TempFile, "");
   SPIRV::constructTranslateCommand(C, *this, JA, Output, TrInput, TrArgs);
 }
